# Upload exclusions for `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# This file must exist. Without it gcloud falls back to .gitignore semantics,
# which happens to work today but is implicit behaviour we should not rely on
# for two things that must never leave the machine:
#
#   * .venv/    - 870 MB, turning a seconds-long upload into a multi-minute one
#   * refrence/ - local reference material, including source PDFs. Gitignored
#                 deliberately; it has no business in a build context either.

.git/
.gitignore

# Local reference material - never upload
refrence/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
*.pem
*.key

# Caches and build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Not needed to build or run the service image
tests/
docs/
terraform/
.github/
# `ui/` is deliberately NOT excluded. It used to be, on the grounds that
# Streamlit must not reach the runtime image - which is true, and is enforced
# where it belongs: the API Dockerfile simply does not COPY it. Excluding it
# from the shared build context instead broke `Dockerfile.ui`, which needs it.
# The directory is ~15KB; bounding context size was never the real motive.
